fb: never present a frame the GPU did not finish; drop it instead (0279)

gpuGateOpen() waits up to 50 ms for the GPU work submitted before the swap, and
then returned "open" anyway. That is how a half-drawn frame reaches the panel:
the still-missing part shows as a horizontal band that drifts with whatever was
left undrawn, which is the moving seam seen on raphael. The gate timeouts were
visible all along as gpu_hold_timeouts.

Return a distinct value for the timeout and drop that frame in swapFired: clear
the pending record, release its holds, and let the panel keep the last complete
frame. The vsync/copy path asks for "== 1" so it cannot present an unfinished
frame either. Count the drops as gpu_drops next to gpu_hold_timeouts.

A dropped frame costs one refresh of motion; presenting an unfinished one shows
a visibly broken picture, so the trade is deliberate.

